1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,100
You walk out of the shop with a twelve-million-dong phone without paying a single dong upfront.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,670
The counter flyer promises zero percent interest over twelve months...

3
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:11,370
yet who really lends money for a whole year for free?

4
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:19,690
The very second you e-sign on the store tablet, your loan skips past the phone shop to an outside finance company.

5
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:25,650
They own the debt contract from now on, even though zero cash has moved between banks yet.

6
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:34,420
Next morning, the finance company wires payout cash to the store, yet only eleven million four hundred thousand lands in their account.

7
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:39,770
The six hundred thousand withheld is a five-percent interest subsidy paid behind the counter.

8
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:45,800
Every month you send back one million until twelve million clears.

9
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:56,410
If cash buyers received six hundred thousand off, you effectively borrowed at zero point eight percent monthly — about ten percent a year.

10
00:00:57,170 --> 00:01:02,650
What if cash buyers and installment shoppers both pay the same twelve million flat?

11
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:09,250
Then you paid zero interest; the shop absorbed six hundred thousand out of markup to close the sale.

12
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:15,970
Next time you spot zero percent, ask one blunt question at the register: what is the cash price right now?

13
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:18,050
Any discount offered is your interest.
